meta {
  name: Override a mark
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attempts/{{attemptId}}/answers/{{firstQuestionId}}/grade
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "awarded_points": 1,
    "feedback": "Marked up by hand — the reasoning was sound."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Back to the **author's** token (`auth: inherit`), because this is the author's act.

  Sets `grader='human'` and **preserves** `llm_rationale`. Keeping the machine's original
  judgement is what makes an override a correction rather than a cover-up: if the mark is
  later disputed, both what the model said and what the human decided are on the record.

  `attempts.score` is re-derived from the answers afterwards. Never store a score that
  cannot be recomputed from its parts.

  Out of range is refused — a three-mark question cannot award four. Audited.
}
